# Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR)

## Task 5 – Complete Pharmacovigilance Case Assessment

## 1. Introduction

An Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR) is a structured report
containing information about a suspected adverse reaction associated
with a medicinal product.

This project presents a complete pharmacovigilance assessment of a
case study. The assessment includes adverse drug reaction
identification, case reporting, causality assessment, seriousness and
expectedness classification, and final case evaluation.

The purpose of this assessment is to simulate the work performed by a
Drug Safety Associate during the processing of an individual safety
case.

---

## 2. Objectives

The objectives of this case assessment are:

- To identify the suspected adverse drug reaction.
- To collect relevant patient information.
- To identify the suspected medicinal product.
- To document the adverse event and its timeline.
- To assess the relationship between the drug and reaction.
- To perform causality assessment.
- To assess seriousness and expectedness.
- To document management and patient outcome.
- To prepare a structured Individual Case Safety Report.
- To understand the importance of pharmacovigilance in patient safety.

