# 20. Drug Safety Associate Perspective

A Drug Safety Associate needs to review safety cases carefully and
ensure that important case information is captured accurately.

Important areas include:

- Patient information
- Reporter information
- Suspected medicine
- Adverse reaction
- Dates
- Medical history
- Concomitant medications
- Investigations
- Causality
- Seriousness
- Expectedness
- Treatment and outcome

The information should be documented clearly so that the case can be
reviewed and followed up when necessary.

---

# 21. Pharmacovigilance Importance

ICSRs are important because individual case reports contribute to
ongoing medicine safety monitoring.

Pharmacovigilance systems collect and evaluate such reports to support
the detection and assessment of potential safety signals.

The WHO Programme for International Drug Monitoring uses ICSRs as an
important source of medicine-safety information, with reports
contributed to the global VigiBase database.

